{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_150021","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder list --repo misty-step/canopy"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"674894f979ce78f3092027edac01eccfdf21f53a\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:11.267Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:142 (instanceParam), server.go:171 (runParam), inventory.go:138 (validateRouteIdentifier), routes GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, GET /fragments/instance, GET /logs. Behaviors: query parameter values for instance must be validated before routing or execution: path traversal (\\\"..\\\", \\\".\\\"), route separators (\\\"/\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\"), control characters, and shell metacharacters must be rejected with HTTP 400 Bad Request across /, /fragments/fleet, /fragments/instance, and /logs. Failing example: invoke GET /?instance=.. or GET /fragments/instance?instance=bad%2Fid or GET /logs?instance=..\\u0026run=run-1; today server_test.go only tests run parameter rejection on /logs (TestHandlerRejectsUnknownAndMalformedRun), leaving instance parameter malformed/traversal validation unexercised on all routes. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in server_test.go asserting that requests with invalid instance parameters (e.g. instance=.., instance=bad/id, instance=bad;id) return HTTP 400 Bad Request across /, /fragments/fleet, /fragments/instance, and /logs. Observed: server.go:150 checks validateRouteIdentifier for instanceParam and returns errBadInstance (status 400), but server_test.go only asserts status 404 for unknown instance and tests no malformed instance parameter. Required: HTTP route regression tests for malformed and traversal instance parameters. Proposed test-work: add server regression tests asserting invalid and traversal instance query parameters return HTTP 400 across all routes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:28:55.422Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:40:32.74Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"done: 674894f979ce78f3092027edac01eccfdf21f53a\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.245Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.245Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nHTTP instance parameters use the shared route-identifier validator before lookup or command execution, but tests cover only an unknown instance and one malformed run ID. The route boundary is not pinned across instance-accepting handlers.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- `/`, `/fragments/fleet`, and `/fragments/instance` allow a missing optional `instance`; `/logs` requires it.\\n- Present-empty or duplicate `instance` values return 400.\\n- Dot/traversal values, Unicode whitespace/control, `/` or `\\\\\\\\`, and the validator's unsafe punctuation classes return 400 before selection or collector execution.\\n- A syntactically valid unknown instance returns 404, not 400.\\n- Missing or malformed `run` on `/logs` returns 400 without calling `Collector.Logs`.\\n- A syntactically valid unknown run reaches the collector and retains the existing 200 unknown-log fragment behavior.\\n- Do not change accepted identifier policy.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven handler test covers every instance-accepting route, parameter cardinality, and each malformed class at least once; every route gets a representative traversal/separator case. A recording collector proves invalid `/logs` requests make zero calls. Keep the existing valid-unknown run assertion. Focused server tests pass.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:05.643Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:40:32.74Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-inventory-validation-bounds\",\n    \"title\": \"Inventory listen address, refresh interval, and empty instance validation lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:19.082Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: inventory.go:59 (validateListen), inventory.go:68-75 (interval validation), inventory.go:76 (empty instances check), called via LoadInventory(path). Behaviors: LoadInventory must validate operational configuration parameters and reject malformed configurations before runtime: (1) listen must be a valid host:port string; values missing a port (e.g. 127.0.0.1), non-numeric ports, out-of-range ports (0 or \\u003e 65535), or containing whitespace/control characters must be rejected; (2) fleet_interval_seconds and selected_interval_seconds must be positive when non-zero; negative intervals (e.g. -1) must be rejected; (3) instances must contain at least one instance; an empty instances array (\\\"instances\\\": []) must be rejected. Failing example: call LoadInventory on JSON with \\\"listen\\\": \\\"127.0.0.1\\\" (missing port) or \\\"fleet_interval_seconds\\\": -5 or \\\"instances\\\": []; today inventory_test.go contains zero tests for listen address syntax, port range boundaries, negative intervals, or empty instance arrays. Acceptance: a Builder adds table-driven unit tests in inventory_test.go asserting that LoadInventory fails with descriptive errors for invalid listen addresses (missing port, port 0, port 70000, whitespace/control chars), negative intervals, and empty instances arrays. Observed: inventory.go:59-78 and inventory.go:87-104 implement validation, but grep confirms no test in inventory_test.go exercises validateListen, negative intervals, or empty instances validation. Required: table-driven regression tests in inventory_test.go covering listen address parsing, port range bounds, negative intervals, and empty instances arrays. Proposed test-work: add table-driven tests in inventory_test.go verifying that LoadInventory rejects invalid listen host:port formats, out-of-range ports, negative intervals, and empty instance arrays.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:10.576Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into if-critic-silent-canopy-config: the meaningful risk is startup silently discarding validation errors. No independent defect found in validateInventory/validateListen; a duplicate helper-validation workstream is not warranted.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:10.758Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:05:24.776Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Real CLI probe of deployed 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6 with explicit -config and JSON listen host containing U+0001: exited 1 with serve: listen tcp: lookup ... no such host. This confirms validateListen does not reject every control character itself, but startup still fails loudly and does not serve or silently fall back. Do not report comprehensive control-character validation as existing behavior. No separate urgent correctness fix promoted: the startup failure contract holds; stricter early diagnostics can be considered with future inventory-boundary work.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:14.306Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:05:24.776Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay\",\n    \"title\": \"Silent instance freshness decay to stale after elapsed maxAge lacks regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:26.217Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: view.go:148 (classifyFreshness), view.go:194 (instanceView), view.go:171 (pageView), routes GET / and GET /fragments/instance. Behaviors: when an instance has a valid prior snapshot (state.Snapshot != nil) and no new error (state.Err == nil), but background collection has not succeeded within the missed-refresh threshold (now \\u003e= LastSuccess + maxAge, where maxAge = 3 * refreshInterval), Canopy must classify its freshness as \\\"stale\\\" and render \\u003cspan class=\\\"status-badge stale\\\"\\u003e and \\u003cspan class=\\\"state-dot stale\\\"\\u003e instead of \\\"fresh\\\". Failing example: construct an App state with a valid snapshot where LastSuccess was 10 minutes ago, Err is nil, and refresh interval is 10s (maxAge = 30s); request GET /fragments/instance?instance=one; today app_test.go:119 (TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure) only tests freshness becoming stale when a collector explicitly returns an error; no test exercises the elapsed time decay where a silent or delayed worker causes freshness to decay from fresh to stale. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in app_test.go and server_test.go verifying that an instance whose last success is older than 3 * refreshInterval is classified as Freshness: \\\"stale\\\" despite Err == nil, and that GET /fragments/instance renders the stale badge. Observed: view.go:155 checks !now.Before(state.LastSuccess.Add(maxAge)), but grep shows this elapsed time decay branch is never tested in any *_test.go file. Required: regression tests in app_test.go and server_test.go covering elapsed-time freshness decay to stale when refresh attempts stall or cease. Proposed test-work: add tests in app_test.go and server_test.go verifying that instances decay to stale freshness when elapsed time exceeds three refresh intervals without a new successful snapshot.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:24.21Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into canopy-critic-stale-selected-window. That bug owns elapsed expiry boundary coverage and preserves silent-worker decay; a separate test pinning 3*refreshInterval would encode the diagnosed defect.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:24.385Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:21.987Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:24.385Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation\",\n    \"title\": \"CLI envelope schema version mismatch and envelope malformed JSON rejection lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.824Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: collector.go:297 (cliCollector.runJSON), collector.go:343 (decodeCLIEnvelope), collector.go:138 (cliCollector.Collect). Behaviors: Canopy relies strictly on the forest.cli.v2 JSON protocol envelope. When a command runner returns an envelope with an invalid or unexpected schema (e.g. \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\"), missing envelope fields (schema, command, args, exit), or trailing JSON data, Collect must reject the envelope with a *CLIError identifying the schema mismatch or envelope error, and terminate collection without accepting invalid data. Failing example: execute collector.Collect where the runner outputs an envelope with Schema: \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\" or with missing schema field or trailing JSON; today collector_test.go only tests command mismatch (TestCLICollectorRejectsEnvelopeCommandMismatch) and exit status failures; zero tests exercise schema mismatch or envelope JSON structural validation. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in collector_test.go asserting that Collect returns a *CLIError with the message mentioning invalid schema when the envelope schema is not \\\"forest.cli.v2\\\", and fails when envelope top-level fields are missing or trailing JSON is present. Observed: collector.go:297-300 and collector.go:356-361 check the schema and top-level envelope fields, but grep reveals no test references invalid schema or envelope field parsing errors. Required: unit tests in collector_test.go covering envelope schema mismatch, missing required envelope keys, and trailing JSON in command output. Proposed test-work: add collector tests in collector_test.go verifying that envelopes with incompatible schema versions, missing top-level keys, or trailing JSON are rejected with a CLIError.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:14:02.396Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"done: a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:28.732Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:14:02.396Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-stale-selected-window\",\n    \"title\": \"Healthy but slow selected instance is rendered stale by the 3x-interval freshness window\",\n    \"spec\": \"Problem: pageView uses 3*refreshInterval as expiry, but refreshLoop waits the interval AFTER collection completes. With default selected interval 2s, snapshots expire after 6s while a legitimate collection can run up to refreshTimeout=30s. This is a missed-refresh signal calculated from an incomplete cycle budget.\\n\\nScope: derive the missed-refresh budget from the configured wait interval plus the existing total collection deadline, with a small documented scheduling allowance. Use existing timing constants and one authoritative calculation; add no persisted duration measurement, extra ticker, or per-instance configuration. Preserve immediate stale on explicit collection error and unknown before any successful snapshot. A silent/stuck worker must still expire even without an error; do not suppress staleness merely because an attempt started. Preserve visible observation timestamps.\\n\\nProof: deterministic time-controlled tests through pageView/real templates show a prior-success selected instance stays fresh beyond the old 6s threshold while within its legitimate cycle budget, becomes stale at the new expiry boundary, and is stale immediately on explicit error. No-success remains unknown. Cover selected/fleet interval changes without sleeps. Exercise one slow-success collector scenario and show eventual successful refresh, with no overlapping collection. Run existing checks. This job owns the elapsed-time regression proposed by canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay; do not pin the obsolete 3x-interval formula.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.656Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: view.go:172 passes maxAge = 3*a.refreshInterval(instance.ID) to instanceView, and view.go:155-157 classifies an instance Stale when now \\u003e= LastSuccess+maxAge even with state.Err == nil. For the selected instance, refreshInterval is SelectedIntervalSeconds (default 2s, inventory.go:27), so the staleness window is 6s. A successful Collect (collector.go:131-208) runs 4+N subprocesses (version, config show, declaration list, one declaration show per declaration, status), each individually bounded by a 30s timeout (collector.go:17, app.go:16), so a healthy selected instance — especially over SSH — can routinely take longer than 6s per cycle. Result: templates/instance.html:16 and fleet.html:21 render the \\\"stale\\\" badge/state-dot for an instance whose collection is succeeding with no error, contradicting the README boundary that stale marks failed/missed refreshes, not healthy ones.\\nRequired: freshness must not report stale for an instance whose refreshes are succeeding; the missed-refresh window must exceed the worst-case collection time for that instance.\\nProposed spec direction: derive maxAge from the collection bound (e.g. refreshTimeout plus margin, or observed last cycle duration) instead of 3x the poll interval, or measure and store per-instance refresh cycle duration; pin with a test where a selected instance with a slow but successful collector renders fresh, not stale.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:59.304Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:47:32.958Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Acceptance clarification: use maxAge = refreshTimeout + 2*refreshInterval(instance.ID). This budgets one configured post-completion wait plus the existing total collection deadline, with one additional configured interval as scheduling allowance; add no new numeric constant or configuration. At now \\u003c LastSuccess+maxAge, a prior-success/no-error state remains fresh; at equality or later it is stale. Explicit errors remain immediately stale and no prior success remains unknown. This replaces the earlier vague allowance language; the active Builder owns implementation.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:52:41.842Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Executive inspection of published revision 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6: app.go introduces freshnessSchedulingSlack=time.Second, which predates/misses the 19:47:32 acceptance clarification. Before approval, replace that extra constant with refreshTimeout + 2*refreshInterval and align boundary expectations. The branch adds 362 lines of freshness tests; retain only distinct observable boundary/error/selection/non-overlap regressions and avoid test plumbing or repeated equivalent paths. This is review feedback on the exact published tip, not approval or a request to bypass Gate.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:56:57.125Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"done: 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:58:31.64Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Executive decision after Gate approval: withdraw the late 19:47:32 formula preference. Accepted release formula is refreshTimeout + refreshInterval + freshnessSchedulingSlack, with the named allowance fixed at time.Second (33s selected, 41s fleet at current defaults). It covers the same required full collection deadline plus configured wait, adds bounded scheduling slack, and preserves silent-worker expiry. No observed correctness defect justifies changing a reviewed working formula merely to match my later preference. Gate approval for 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6 explicitly verifies this calculation. This supersedes the formula correction requested at 19:52:41; retain behavior-focused tests.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:02.78Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:02.78Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: pageView uses 3*refreshInterval as expiry, but refreshLoop waits the interval AFTER collection completes. With default selected interval 2s, snapshots expire after 6s while a legitimate collection can run up to refreshTimeout=30s. This is a missed-refresh signal calculated from an incomplete cycle budget.\\n\\nScope: derive the missed-refresh budget from the configured wait interval plus the existing total collection deadline, with a small documented scheduling allowance. Use existing timing constants and one authoritative calculation; add no persisted duration measurement, extra ticker, or per-instance configuration. Preserve immediate stale on explicit collection error and unknown before any successful snapshot. A silent/stuck worker must still expire even without an error; do not suppress staleness merely because an attempt started. Preserve visible observation timestamps.\\n\\nProof: deterministic time-controlled tests through pageView/real templates show a prior-success selected instance stays fresh beyond the old 6s threshold while within its legitimate cycle budget, becomes stale at the new expiry boundary, and is stale immediately on explicit error. No-success remains unknown. Cover selected/fleet interval changes without sleeps. Exercise one slow-success collector scenario and show eventual successful refresh, with no overlapping collection. Run existing checks. This job owns the elapsed-time regression proposed by canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay; do not pin the obsolete 3x-interval formula.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.492Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:58:31.64Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision\",\n    \"title\": \"Discovery ID collisions silently drop discoverable Forest instances\",\n    \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:56:11.467Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.828Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: discovery.go:16 keys discovered candidates by root path, so DiscoverLocalInstances can return multiple instances whose sanitized IDs collide: sanitizeID (discovery.go:196-210) maps \\\"agent_test\\\" and \\\"agent-beta\\\" style names to the same ID (both \\\"agent-test\\\", underscores and dashes both normalize to \\\"-\\\"). app.go:239-241 then builds discMap keyed by instance ID, so the second colliding instance silently overwrites the first in the map and, at app.go:275-283, is skipped via existingMap — a working Forest checkout simply never appears in the fleet, with no log or error. The same silent-drop applies if a discovered ID matches an explicit inventory ID.\\nRequired: every discoverable, validated instance must either appear in the fleet or its omission must be surfaced; discovery IDs must be unique per instance or collisions must be resolved deterministically and observably.\\nProposed spec direction: make DiscoverLocalInstances deduplicate or disambiguate by ID (e.g. suffix the ID from the root path on collision) before returning, or make syncDiscoveredInstances log/record dropped collisions; add a discovery test with two sibling dirs whose names sanitize to the same ID.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:56:11.467Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:31:56.483Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Blocking executive review of exact revision 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267; two independent reproductions run in an isolated git-archive checkout against actual source, go test -run TestExecutive -count=1 . exited 1. (1) syncDiscoveredInstances with A={ID:x,Root:/tmp/a} and B={ID:x,Root:/tmp/b}, then a scan containing only B: surviving route changes x-2 -\\u003e x. Counter assignment is topology-dependent; rebuilding it each scan breaks route-to-root stability and can retain the old x worker/state under a different root. Preserve existing discovered endpoint identity during reconciliation, then allocate only new identities; test removal, addition, and reappearance, not just reversed simultaneous inputs. (2) resolveDiscoveryCollisions with local Root=/srv/forest and explicit Host=other.example,Root=/srv/forest returns zero discovered entries. explicitRoots is keyed only by path, so an unrelated SSH target hides the local checkout. Include transport/host in endpoint equality; only an explicit local entry for the same local root may suppress its discovery. Tests added on the branch cover same-host duplicates and fixed-set reordering but neither failing transition. Both failures reproduced in 0.002s; no source changes applied to branch, no Gate verdict fabricated. Required correction belongs to this existing job. Also remove tests pinning -2 counter allocation rather than the stable-identity contract.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.665Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:31:56.483Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": true\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-auditstatus-dead-surface\",\n    \"title\": \"TriggerViewModel.AuditStatus is computed but never rendered\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.987Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: view.go:61 declares TriggerViewModel.AuditStatus and view.go:344 computes it via triggerStatus(trigger.StateKnown, trigger.AuditError), but no template renders it (grep over templates/*.html shows zero references to AuditStatus) and no test asserts it. The trigger matrix in instance.html renders only PollStatus, RunStatus, and ConsecutiveErrors; AuditError reaches the UI only through the aggregated Errors list (view.go:262-268). This is unused computed surface: it costs a maintenance obligation on every triggerStatus change while contributing nothing observable.\\nRequired: shipped view surface is either consumed by a rendered behavior or removed; per repository conventions the projection should not carry unrendered derived fields.\\nProposed spec direction: either delete TriggerViewModel.AuditStatus and its assignment, or render an Audit column in the trigger matrix if the operator surface is meant to show per-trigger audit state; note the semantics question that view.go:344 reuses StateKnown (poll state) for audit status, which needs its own known flag if rendered.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:23.747Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into if-critic-dead-collector-surface; confirmed unused AuditStatus computation. Preserve visible AuditError aggregation; no new audit UI required.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:23.926Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.827Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:23.926Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-trigger-matrix-warnings\",\n    \"title\": \"Instance trigger matrix status badges and collection warnings rendering lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:39.502Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: view.go:245-260 (instanceView), view.go:332-348 (triggerViews), templates/instance.html:10-16 (Collection warnings), templates/instance.html:66-77 (Trigger matrix), route GET /fragments/instance. Behaviors: when an instance snapshot contains Kernel lock errors (snapshot.Status.Kernel.LockError), trigger state errors, or trigger poll/run/audit errors: (1) Canopy must render the \\\"Collection warnings\\\" card (\\u003ch2 id=\\\"instance-errors\\\"\\u003eCollection warnings\\u003c/h2\\u003e) with \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003eattention\\u003c/span\\u003e listing each warning; (2) in the \\\"Trigger matrix\\\" table, each trigger row must render the trigger name, poll status badge (\\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003e on poll error, \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal stale\\\"\\u003e when trigger.Stale, \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal unknown\\\"\\u003e when not StateKnown), run status badge, and consecutive errors count. Failing example: create a snapshot with Status.Kernel.LockError = \\\"lock held by pid 42\\\", a trigger with PollError = \\\"connection refused\\\" and ConsecutiveErrors = 2, and a trigger with Stale = true; request GET /fragments/instance?instance=one; today server_test.go contains zero assertions for collection warnings or trigger matrix poll/run/stale signal classes. Acceptance: a Builder adds an HTTP handler test in server_test.go verifying that GET /fragments/instance renders the \\\"Collection warnings\\\" card containing lock and trigger error text, and renders the expected signal badges (class=\\\"signal error\\\", class=\\\"signal stale\\\") in the Trigger matrix table. Observed: view.go:245-260 populates view.Errors from lock and trigger errors and view.go:345 sets PollStatus = \\\"stale\\\", but grep confirms LockError, PollError, and trigger signal badges are never tested in server_test.go. Required: HTTP handler regression tests in server_test.go proving that kernel lock errors, trigger poll errors, and stale trigger states render correctly in Collection warnings and the Trigger matrix. Proposed test-work: add server regression tests asserting that kernel lock errors, trigger poll errors, and stale trigger states render in Collection warnings and the Trigger matrix table.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:53:11.184Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into if-critic-dead-collector-surface because its planned AuditStatus deletion is the concrete regression risk. Existing warnings must remain visible; a standalone suite pinning markup and copied fields adds maintenance without a separate demonstrated defect.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:53:11.341Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:35.03Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:53:11.341Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-log-general-error-fragment\",\n    \"title\": \"Run log general collector failure error fragment rendering lacks regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:46.221Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: server.go:121 (handleLogs), templates/log.html:18 (error state card), route GET /logs. Behaviors: when GET /logs?instance=\\u003cid\\u003e\\u0026run=\\u003cid\\u003e is requested and Collector.Logs returns a non-exit-4 failure (e.g. process exit 1, I/O error, or timeout), Canopy must return HTTP 200 with the log drawer fragment rendering State = \\\"error\\\", badge \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003eerror\\u003c/span\\u003e, headline \\u003cp\\u003eCanopy could not read this Run log.\\u003c/p\\u003e, and the error message in \\u003cp class=\\\"muted\\\"\\u003e, without returning an HTTP 500 error or panicking. Failing example: configure collector.logs to return errors.New(\\\"ssh connection reset by peer\\\") or \\u0026CLIError{Command: \\\"run logs\\\", Exit: 1, Message: \\\"database disk image is malformed\\\"} and request GET /logs?instance=one\\u0026run=run-1; today server_test.go:37 (TestHandlerRejectsUnknownAndMalformedRun) covers exit 4 (\\\"unknown\\\") and malformed query params, and TestHandlerMapsEvictedLogToFragmentState covers evicted logs, but the general collector error rendering path is unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds a test in server_test.go verifying that when Collector.Logs returns a non-exit-4 error, GET /logs returns HTTP 200, renders state \\\"error\\\" with \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003eerror\\u003c/span\\u003e, and displays the collector error message. Observed: server.go:121-124 assigns view.State = \\\"error\\\" on general collector failure, but grep shows server_test.go never tests GET /logs with a failing collector other than exit 4. Required: an HTTP regression test in server_test.go verifying that general collector errors during log fetching render the error fragment with HTTP 200. Proposed test-work: add a server test in server_test.go verifying that GET /logs returns HTTP 200 and renders the error state fragment when Collector.Logs encounters a non-exit-4 failure.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:11.121Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into active canopy-log-drawer-experience. Pinning current inline markup and headline would be obsolete during drawer redesign; its observable ordinary-error behavior belongs to that owner.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:11.301Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:41.833Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:11.301Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-publication-primary-refresh\",\n    \"title\": \"Preserve pre-publication primary refresh in Builder and Fixer policy\",\n    \"spec\": \"Make the proven local pre-publication primary-refresh policy durable through a normal exact-revision review request. Scope only agents/builder/agent.md and agents/fixer/agent.md (or their established shared owner if current primary already centralizes this policy). Build from current origin primary; do not copy dirty main-checkout files wholesale or import unrelated operational edits.\\n\\nBefore preparing review-request payloads, both roles must fetch origin and require the final checked revision to contain origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}. If stale, rebase their subject/repair onto the fetched primary, preserve both feature and primary behavior, and rerun every configured check before publishing the resulting SHA. Failed rebase/check stops publication. Fixer must retain the original rejected SHA for Kernel compare-and-swap. Preserve Kernel atomic publication and the Verifier/Gate ancestry check: this guard reduces avoidable stale publication but cannot eliminate later races. Add no scheduler, retry loop, dependency, new role, or Kernel code.\\n\\nEvidence: collision revision 34b04b06de58ebfe735dedd977b00c2a614cc752 passed checks but was stale because 73d1489 landed during implementation. Local Fixer policy digest 4d7e25ef73d3dad94e08d461a7347a6c4cde500e195c81bd3d60d4c547671c32 was exercised by Run 1788552644310643252-fixer: it refetched, verified ancestry, and published 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 with original rejected-SHA CAS.\\n\\nAcceptance: reviewable minimal role-policy diff on current primary; supported forest declaration show loads both declarations without errors; repository checks pass; exact request/verdict/Gate evidence integrates the policy. Do not add source-text tests for prompts or claim local runtime hashes prove Git integration.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-05T00:21:29.67Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:17:54.108Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Execution prerequisite observed after promotion: Canopy Verifier Run 1788552943774438475-verifier failed on OpenRouter 402 for a 384000-token output reservation, before publishing any verdict. Shared root-cause job is misty-step/iron-forest:if-provider-output-ceiling. This is not a code/check rejection and does not invalidate prior exact approvals. Keep this job takeable for Builder implementation; integration needs a successful provider-backed Verifier Run. Do not change transport credentials or bypass Gate to complete it.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:21:29.67Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:28:25.63Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Post-publication integration diagnosis: real service-environment forest poll verifier returns 0 (ready), while supported trigger show verifier reports run_error=\\\"provider budget exhausted\\\" and no active Run. Kernel service is active. Thus the pending eebc1cc9968e3eb37715549d78fc9d0a233553a1 review is not stranded by Powder scope or lack of request work; provider admission is the current hold. Do not reset/bypass the guard without fixing admission. Shared output-ceiling job remains unclaimed at the last read.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Make the proven local pre-publication primary-refresh policy durable through a normal exact-revision review request. Scope only agents/builder/agent.md and agents/fixer/agent.md (or their established shared owner if current primary already centralizes this policy). Build from current origin primary; do not copy dirty main-checkout files wholesale or import unrelated operational edits.\\n\\nBefore preparing review-request payloads, both roles must fetch origin and require the final checked revision to contain origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}. If stale, rebase their subject/repair onto the fetched primary, preserve both feature and primary behavior, and rerun every configured check before publishing the resulting SHA. Failed rebase/check stops publication. Fixer must retain the original rejected SHA for Kernel compare-and-swap. Preserve Kernel atomic publication and the Verifier/Gate ancestry check: this guard reduces avoidable stale publication but cannot eliminate later races. Add no scheduler, retry loop, dependency, new role, or Kernel code.\\n\\nEvidence: collision revision 34b04b06de58ebfe735dedd977b00c2a614cc752 passed checks but was stale because 73d1489 landed during implementation. Local Fixer policy digest 4d7e25ef73d3dad94e08d461a7347a6c4cde500e195c81bd3d60d4c547671c32 was exercised by Run 1788552644310643252-fixer: it refetched, verified ancestry, and published 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 with original rejected-SHA CAS.\\n\\nAcceptance: reviewable minimal role-policy diff on current primary; supported forest declaration show loads both declarations without errors; repository checks pass; exact request/verdict/Gate evidence integrates the policy. Do not add source-text tests for prompts or claim local runtime hashes prove Git integration.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:28:25.63Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": true\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-verifier-current-subject\",\n    \"title\": \"Read current Powder contract and review evidence before verdict publication\",\n    \"spec\": \"Make current Subject feedback an explicit read-only Verifier input in agents/verifier/agent.md. For request tracker=powder, read powder show \\u003csubject\\u003e before reviewing and again immediately before publishing a verdict; require matching repository, current spec, and notes. Reconcile conflicting instructions or reproductions explicitly against behavior rather than silently ignoring or blindly accepting them. If the current Subject contract cannot be read, do not approve. Do not acquire, release, or complete its claim. Preserve exact-revision request provenance, configured checks, and Gate ancestry requirements; GitHub requests must not invoke Powder.\\n\\nReason: the pending collision revision 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 has two experimentally reproduced blockers added after publication (route reassignment on disappearance; remote path suppresses local discovery). The local Verifier declaration previously only said available actionable review feedback without naming how to obtain current Powder notes. Local operational change already loads as digest 97d73b32c0d5abeba4daf78670218f651bbfb9960c710c0c4dfbefd0a8e7b9d5; make only this policy durable from current primary, without copying unrelated dirty main-checkout changes.\\n\\nProof: declaration show accepts the changed Verifier policy; configured checks pass; normal exact-revision review request and Gate integrate it. No source-text tests for prompts. In subsequent real review, retain evidence of read-only current Subject lookup and disposition of actionable notes. Keep policy-only change small; no new state, tools, credentials, or Kernel mechanisms.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-05T00:36:14.926Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:36:14.926Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:33:20.929Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:33:20.929Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Make current Subject feedback an explicit read-only Verifier input in agents/verifier/agent.md. For request tracker=powder, read powder show \\u003csubject\\u003e before reviewing and again immediately before publishing a verdict; require matching repository, current spec, and notes. Reconcile conflicting instructions or reproductions explicitly against behavior rather than silently ignoring or blindly accepting them. If the current Subject contract cannot be read, do not approve. Do not acquire, release, or complete its claim. Preserve exact-revision request provenance, configured checks, and Gate ancestry requirements; GitHub requests must not invoke Powder.\\n\\nReason: the pending collision revision 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 has two experimentally reproduced blockers added after publication (route reassignment on disappearance; remote path suppresses local discovery). The local Verifier declaration previously only said available actionable review feedback without naming how to obtain current Powder notes. Local operational change already loads as digest 97d73b32c0d5abeba4daf78670218f651bbfb9960c710c0c4dfbefd0a8e7b9d5; make only this policy durable from current primary, without copying unrelated dirty main-checkout changes.\\n\\nProof: declaration show accepts the changed Verifier policy; configured checks pass; normal exact-revision review request and Gate integrate it. No source-text tests for prompts. In subsequent real review, retain evidence of read-only current Subject lookup and disposition of actionable notes. Keep policy-only change small; no new state, tools, credentials, or Kernel mechanisms.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:33:20.929Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:36:14.926Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": true\n    }\n  }\n]"}],"details":{"truncation":{"content":"    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"674894f979ce78f3092027edac01eccfdf21f53a\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:11.267Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:142 (instanceParam), server.go:171 (runParam), inventory.go:138 (validateRouteIdentifier), routes GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, GET /fragments/instance, GET /logs. Behaviors: query parameter values for instance must be validated before routing or execution: path traversal (\\\"..\\\", \\\".\\\"), route separators (\\\"/\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\"), control characters, and shell metacharacters must be rejected with HTTP 400 Bad Request across /, /fragments/fleet, /fragments/instance, and /logs. Failing example: invoke GET /?instance=.. or GET /fragments/instance?instance=bad%2Fid or GET /logs?instance=..\\u0026run=run-1; today server_test.go only tests run parameter rejection on /logs (TestHandlerRejectsUnknownAndMalformedRun), leaving instance parameter malformed/traversal validation unexercised on all routes. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in server_test.go asserting that requests with invalid instance parameters (e.g. instance=.., instance=bad/id, instance=bad;id) return HTTP 400 Bad Request across /, /fragments/fleet, /fragments/instance, and /logs. Observed: server.go:150 checks validateRouteIdentifier for instanceParam and returns errBadInstance (status 400), but server_test.go only asserts status 404 for unknown instance and tests no malformed instance parameter. Required: HTTP route regression tests for malformed and traversal instance parameters. Proposed test-work: add server regression tests asserting invalid and traversal instance query parameters return HTTP 400 across all routes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:28:55.422Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:40:32.74Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"done: 674894f979ce78f3092027edac01eccfdf21f53a\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.245Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.245Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nHTTP instance parameters use the shared route-identifier validator before lookup or command execution, but tests cover only an unknown instance and one malformed run ID. The route boundary is not pinned across instance-accepting handlers.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- `/`, `/fragments/fleet`, and `/fragments/instance` allow a missing optional `instance`; `/logs` requires it.\\n- Present-empty or duplicate `instance` values return 400.\\n- Dot/traversal values, Unicode whitespace/control, `/` or `\\\\\\\\`, and the validator's unsafe punctuation classes return 400 before selection or collector execution.\\n- A syntactically valid unknown instance returns 404, not 400.\\n- Missing or malformed `run` on `/logs` returns 400 without calling `Collector.Logs`.\\n- A syntactically valid unknown run reaches the collector and retains the existing 200 unknown-log fragment behavior.\\n- Do not change accepted identifier policy.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven handler test covers every instance-accepting route, parameter cardinality, and each malformed class at least once; every route gets a representative traversal/separator case. A recording collector proves invalid `/logs` requests make zero calls. Keep the existing valid-unknown run assertion. Focused server tests pass.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:05.643Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:40:32.74Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-inventory-validation-bounds\",\n    \"title\": \"Inventory listen address, refresh interval, and empty instance validation lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:19.082Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: inventory.go:59 (validateListen), inventory.go:68-75 (interval validation), inventory.go:76 (empty instances check), called via LoadInventory(path). Behaviors: LoadInventory must validate operational configuration parameters and reject malformed configurations before runtime: (1) listen must be a valid host:port string; values missing a port (e.g. 127.0.0.1), non-numeric ports, out-of-range ports (0 or \\u003e 65535), or containing whitespace/control characters must be rejected; (2) fleet_interval_seconds and selected_interval_seconds must be positive when non-zero; negative intervals (e.g. -1) must be rejected; (3) instances must contain at least one instance; an empty instances array (\\\"instances\\\": []) must be rejected. Failing example: call LoadInventory on JSON with \\\"listen\\\": \\\"127.0.0.1\\\" (missing port) or \\\"fleet_interval_seconds\\\": -5 or \\\"instances\\\": []; today inventory_test.go contains zero tests for listen address syntax, port range boundaries, negative intervals, or empty instance arrays. Acceptance: a Builder adds table-driven unit tests in inventory_test.go asserting that LoadInventory fails with descriptive errors for invalid listen addresses (missing port, port 0, port 70000, whitespace/control chars), negative intervals, and empty instances arrays. Observed: inventory.go:59-78 and inventory.go:87-104 implement validation, but grep confirms no test in inventory_test.go exercises validateListen, negative intervals, or empty instances validation. Required: table-driven regression tests in inventory_test.go covering listen address parsing, port range bounds, negative intervals, and empty instances arrays. Proposed test-work: add table-driven tests in inventory_test.go verifying that LoadInventory rejects invalid listen host:port formats, out-of-range ports, negative intervals, and empty instance arrays.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:10.576Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into if-critic-silent-canopy-config: the meaningful risk is startup silently discarding validation errors. No independent defect found in validateInventory/validateListen; a duplicate helper-validation workstream is not warranted.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:10.758Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:05:24.776Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Real CLI probe of deployed 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6 with explicit -config and JSON listen host containing U+0001: exited 1 with serve: listen tcp: lookup ... no such host. This confirms validateListen does not reject every control character itself, but startup still fails loudly and does not serve or silently fall back. Do not report comprehensive control-character validation as existing behavior. No separate urgent correctness fix promoted: the startup failure contract holds; stricter early diagnostics can be considered with future inventory-boundary work.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:14.306Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:05:24.776Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay\",\n    \"title\": \"Silent instance freshness decay to stale after elapsed maxAge lacks regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:26.217Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: view.go:148 (classifyFreshness), view.go:194 (instanceView), view.go:171 (pageView), routes GET / and GET /fragments/instance. Behaviors: when an instance has a valid prior snapshot (state.Snapshot != nil) and no new error (state.Err == nil), but background collection has not succeeded within the missed-refresh threshold (now \\u003e= LastSuccess + maxAge, where maxAge = 3 * refreshInterval), Canopy must classify its freshness as \\\"stale\\\" and render \\u003cspan class=\\\"status-badge stale\\\"\\u003e and \\u003cspan class=\\\"state-dot stale\\\"\\u003e instead of \\\"fresh\\\". Failing example: construct an App state with a valid snapshot where LastSuccess was 10 minutes ago, Err is nil, and refresh interval is 10s (maxAge = 30s); request GET /fragments/instance?instance=one; today app_test.go:119 (TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure) only tests freshness becoming stale when a collector explicitly returns an error; no test exercises the elapsed time decay where a silent or delayed worker causes freshness to decay from fresh to stale. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in app_test.go and server_test.go verifying that an instance whose last success is older than 3 * refreshInterval is classified as Freshness: \\\"stale\\\" despite Err == nil, and that GET /fragments/instance renders the stale badge. Observed: view.go:155 checks !now.Before(state.LastSuccess.Add(maxAge)), but grep shows this elapsed time decay branch is never tested in any *_test.go file. Required: regression tests in app_test.go and server_test.go covering elapsed-time freshness decay to stale when refresh attempts stall or cease. Proposed test-work: add tests in app_test.go and server_test.go verifying that instances decay to stale freshness when elapsed time exceeds three refresh intervals without a new successful snapshot.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:24.21Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into canopy-critic-stale-selected-window. That bug owns elapsed expiry boundary coverage and preserves silent-worker decay; a separate test pinning 3*refreshInterval would encode the diagnosed defect.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:24.385Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:21.987Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:24.385Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation\",\n    \"title\": \"CLI envelope schema version mismatch and envelope malformed JSON rejection lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.824Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: collector.go:297 (cliCollector.runJSON), collector.go:343 (decodeCLIEnvelope), collector.go:138 (cliCollector.Collect). Behaviors: Canopy relies strictly on the forest.cli.v2 JSON protocol envelope. When a command runner returns an envelope with an invalid or unexpected schema (e.g. \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\"), missing envelope fields (schema, command, args, exit), or trailing JSON data, Collect must reject the envelope with a *CLIError identifying the schema mismatch or envelope error, and terminate collection without accepting invalid data. Failing example: execute collector.Collect where the runner outputs an envelope with Schema: \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\" or with missing schema field or trailing JSON; today collector_test.go only tests command mismatch (TestCLICollectorRejectsEnvelopeCommandMismatch) and exit status failures; zero tests exercise schema mismatch or envelope JSON structural validation. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in collector_test.go asserting that Collect returns a *CLIError with the message mentioning invalid schema when the envelope schema is not \\\"forest.cli.v2\\\", and fails when envelope top-level fields are missing or trailing JSON is present. Observed: collector.go:297-300 and collector.go:356-361 check the schema and top-level envelope fields, but grep reveals no test references invalid schema or envelope field parsing errors. Required: unit tests in collector_test.go covering envelope schema mismatch, missing required envelope keys, and trailing JSON in command output. Proposed test-work: add collector tests in collector_test.go verifying that envelopes with incompatible schema versions, missing top-level keys, or trailing JSON are rejected with a CLIError.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:14:02.396Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"done: a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:28.732Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:14:02.396Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-stale-selected-window\",\n    \"title\": \"Healthy but slow selected instance is rendered stale by the 3x-interval freshness window\",\n    \"spec\": \"Problem: pageView uses 3*refreshInterval as expiry, but refreshLoop waits the interval AFTER collection completes. With default selected interval 2s, snapshots expire after 6s while a legitimate collection can run up to refreshTimeout=30s. This is a missed-refresh signal calculated from an incomplete cycle budget.\\n\\nScope: derive the missed-refresh budget from the configured wait interval plus the existing total collection deadline, with a small documented scheduling allowance. Use existing timing constants and one authoritative calculation; add no persisted duration measurement, extra ticker, or per-instance configuration. Preserve immediate stale on explicit collection error and unknown before any successful snapshot. A silent/stuck worker must still expire even without an error; do not suppress staleness merely because an attempt started. Preserve visible observation timestamps.\\n\\nProof: deterministic time-controlled tests through pageView/real templates show a prior-success selected instance stays fresh beyond the old 6s threshold while within its legitimate cycle budget, becomes stale at the new expiry boundary, and is stale immediately on explicit error. No-success remains unknown. Cover selected/fleet interval changes without sleeps. Exercise one slow-success collector scenario and show eventual successful refresh, with no overlapping collection. Run existing checks. This job owns the elapsed-time regression proposed by canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay; do not pin the obsolete 3x-interval formula.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.656Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: view.go:172 passes maxAge = 3*a.refreshInterval(instance.ID) to instanceView, and view.go:155-157 classifies an instance Stale when now \\u003e= LastSuccess+maxAge even with state.Err == nil. For the selected instance, refreshInterval is SelectedIntervalSeconds (default 2s, inventory.go:27), so the staleness window is 6s. A successful Collect (collector.go:131-208) runs 4+N subprocesses (version, config show, declaration list, one declaration show per declaration, status), each individually bounded by a 30s timeout (collector.go:17, app.go:16), so a healthy selected instance — especially over SSH — can routinely take longer than 6s per cycle. Result: templates/instance.html:16 and fleet.html:21 render the \\\"stale\\\" badge/state-dot for an instance whose collection is succeeding with no error, contradicting the README boundary that stale marks failed/missed refreshes, not healthy ones.\\nRequired: freshness must not report stale for an instance whose refreshes are succeeding; the missed-refresh window must exceed the worst-case collection time for that instance.\\nProposed spec direction: derive maxAge from the collection bound (e.g. refreshTimeout plus margin, or observed last cycle duration) instead of 3x the poll interval, or measure and store per-instance refresh cycle duration; pin with a test where a selected instance with a slow but successful collector renders fresh, not stale.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:59.304Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:47:32.958Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Acceptance clarification: use maxAge = refreshTimeout + 2*refreshInterval(instance.ID). This budgets one configured post-completion wait plus the existing total collection deadline, with one additional configured interval as scheduling allowance; add no new numeric constant or configuration. At now \\u003c LastSuccess+maxAge, a prior-success/no-error state remains fresh; at equality or later it is stale. Explicit errors remain immediately stale and no prior success remains unknown. This replaces the earlier vague allowance language; the active Builder owns implementation.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:52:41.842Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Executive inspection of published revision 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6: app.go introduces freshnessSchedulingSlack=time.Second, which predates/misses the 19:47:32 acceptance clarification. Before approval, replace that extra constant with refreshTimeout + 2*refreshInterval and align boundary expectations. The branch adds 362 lines of freshness tests; retain only distinct observable boundary/error/selection/non-overlap regressions and avoid test plumbing or repeated equivalent paths. This is review feedback on the exact published tip, not approval or a request to bypass Gate.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:56:57.125Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"done: 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:58:31.64Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Executive decision after Gate approval: withdraw the late 19:47:32 formula preference. Accepted release formula is refreshTimeout + refreshInterval + freshnessSchedulingSlack, with the named allowance fixed at time.Second (33s selected, 41s fleet at current defaults). It covers the same required full collection deadline plus configured wait, adds bounded scheduling slack, and preserves silent-worker expiry. No observed correctness defect justifies changing a reviewed working formula merely to match my later preference. Gate approval for 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6 explicitly verifies this calculation. This supersedes the formula correction requested at 19:52:41; retain behavior-focused tests.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:02.78Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:02.78Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: pageView uses 3*refreshInterval as expiry, but refreshLoop waits the interval AFTER collection completes. With default selected interval 2s, snapshots expire after 6s while a legitimate collection can run up to refreshTimeout=30s. This is a missed-refresh signal calculated from an incomplete cycle budget.\\n\\nScope: derive the missed-refresh budget from the configured wait interval plus the existing total collection deadline, with a small documented scheduling allowance. Use existing timing constants and one authoritative calculation; add no persisted duration measurement, extra ticker, or per-instance configuration. Preserve immediate stale on explicit collection error and unknown before any successful snapshot. A silent/stuck worker must still expire even without an error; do not suppress staleness merely because an attempt started. Preserve visible observation timestamps.\\n\\nProof: deterministic time-controlled tests through pageView/real templates show a prior-success selected instance stays fresh beyond the old 6s threshold while within its legitimate cycle budget, becomes stale at the new expiry boundary, and is stale immediately on explicit error. No-success remains unknown. Cover selected/fleet interval changes without sleeps. Exercise one slow-success collector scenario and show eventual successful refresh, with no overlapping collection. Run existing checks. This job owns the elapsed-time regression proposed by canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay; do not pin the obsolete 3x-interval formula.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.492Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:58:31.64Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision\",\n    \"title\": \"Discovery ID collisions silently drop discoverable Forest instances\",\n    \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:56:11.467Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.828Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: discovery.go:16 keys discovered candidates by root path, so DiscoverLocalInstances can return multiple instances whose sanitized IDs collide: sanitizeID (discovery.go:196-210) maps \\\"agent_test\\\" and \\\"agent-beta\\\" style names to the same ID (both \\\"agent-test\\\", underscores and dashes both normalize to \\\"-\\\"). app.go:239-241 then builds discMap keyed by instance ID, so the second colliding instance silently overwrites the first in the map and, at app.go:275-283, is skipped via existingMap — a working Forest checkout simply never appears in the fleet, with no log or error. The same silent-drop applies if a discovered ID matches an explicit inventory ID.\\nRequired: every discoverable, validated instance must either appear in the fleet or its omission must be surfaced; discovery IDs must be unique per instance or collisions must be resolved deterministically and observably.\\nProposed spec direction: make DiscoverLocalInstances deduplicate or disambiguate by ID (e.g. suffix the ID from the root path on collision) before returning, or make syncDiscoveredInstances log/record dropped collisions; add a discovery test with two sibling dirs whose names sanitize to the same ID.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:56:11.467Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:31:56.483Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Blocking executive review of exact revision 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267; two independent reproductions run in an isolated git-archive checkout against actual source, go test -run TestExecutive -count=1 . exited 1. (1) syncDiscoveredInstances with A={ID:x,Root:/tmp/a} and B={ID:x,Root:/tmp/b}, then a scan containing only B: surviving route changes x-2 -\\u003e x. Counter assignment is topology-dependent; rebuilding it each scan breaks route-to-root stability and can retain the old x worker/state under a different root. Preserve existing discovered endpoint identity during reconciliation, then allocate only new identities; test removal, addition, and reappearance, not just reversed simultaneous inputs. (2) resolveDiscoveryCollisions with local Root=/srv/forest and explicit Host=other.example,Root=/srv/forest returns zero discovered entries. explicitRoots is keyed only by path, so an unrelated SSH target hides the local checkout. Include transport/host in endpoint equality; only an explicit local entry for the same local root may suppress its discovery. Tests added on the branch cover same-host duplicates and fixed-set reordering but neither failing transition. Both failures reproduced in 0.002s; no source changes applied to branch, no Gate verdict fabricated. Required correction belongs to this existing job. Also remove tests pinning -2 counter allocation rather than the stable-identity contract.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.665Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:31:56.483Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": true\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-auditstatus-dead-surface\",\n    \"title\": \"TriggerViewModel.AuditStatus is computed but never rendered\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.987Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: view.go:61 declares TriggerViewModel.AuditStatus and view.go:344 computes it via triggerStatus(trigger.StateKnown, trigger.AuditError), but no template renders it (grep over templates/*.html shows zero references to AuditStatus) and no test asserts it. The trigger matrix in instance.html renders only PollStatus, RunStatus, and ConsecutiveErrors; AuditError reaches the UI only through the aggregated Errors list (view.go:262-268). This is unused computed surface: it costs a maintenance obligation on every triggerStatus change while contributing nothing observable.\\nRequired: shipped view surface is either consumed by a rendered behavior or removed; per repository conventions the projection should not carry unrendered derived fields.\\nProposed spec direction: either delete TriggerViewModel.AuditStatus and its assignment, or render an Audit column in the trigger matrix if the operator surface is meant to show per-trigger audit state; note the semantics question that view.go:344 reuses StateKnown (poll state) for audit status, which needs its own known flag if rendered.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:23.747Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into if-critic-dead-collector-surface; confirmed unused AuditStatus computation. Preserve visible AuditError aggregation; no new audit UI required.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:23.926Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.827Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:23.926Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-trigger-matrix-warnings\",\n    \"title\": \"Instance trigger matrix status badges and collection warnings rendering lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:39.502Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: view.go:245-260 (instanceView), view.go:332-348 (triggerViews), templates/instance.html:10-16 (Collection warnings), templates/instance.html:66-77 (Trigger matrix), route GET /fragments/instance. Behaviors: when an instance snapshot contains Kernel lock errors (snapshot.Status.Kernel.LockError), trigger state errors, or trigger poll/run/audit errors: (1) Canopy must render the \\\"Collection warnings\\\" card (\\u003ch2 id=\\\"instance-errors\\\"\\u003eCollection warnings\\u003c/h2\\u003e) with \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003eattention\\u003c/span\\u003e listing each warning; (2) in the \\\"Trigger matrix\\\" table, each trigger row must render the trigger name, poll status badge (\\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003e on poll error, \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal stale\\\"\\u003e when trigger.Stale, \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal unknown\\\"\\u003e when not StateKnown), run status badge, and consecutive errors count. Failing example: create a snapshot with Status.Kernel.LockError = \\\"lock held by pid 42\\\", a trigger with PollError = \\\"connection refused\\\" and ConsecutiveErrors = 2, and a trigger with Stale = true; request GET /fragments/instance?instance=one; today server_test.go contains zero assertions for collection warnings or trigger matrix poll/run/stale signal classes. Acceptance: a Builder adds an HTTP handler test in server_test.go verifying that GET /fragments/instance renders the \\\"Collection warnings\\\" card containing lock and trigger error text, and renders the expected signal badges (class=\\\"signal error\\\", class=\\\"signal stale\\\") in the Trigger matrix table. Observed: view.go:245-260 populates view.Errors from lock and trigger errors and view.go:345 sets PollStatus = \\\"stale\\\", but grep confirms LockError, PollError, and trigger signal badges are never tested in server_test.go. Required: HTTP handler regression tests in server_test.go proving that kernel lock errors, trigger poll errors, and stale trigger states render correctly in Collection warnings and the Trigger matrix. Proposed test-work: add server regression tests asserting that kernel lock errors, trigger poll errors, and stale trigger states render in Collection warnings and the Trigger matrix table.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:53:11.184Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into if-critic-dead-collector-surface because its planned AuditStatus deletion is the concrete regression risk. Existing warnings must remain visible; a standalone suite pinning markup and copied fields adds maintenance without a separate demonstrated defect.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:53:11.341Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"abandoned\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": null,\n    \"promoted_at\": null,\n    \"promotions\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:35.03Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:53:11.341Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": true,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": false,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-log-general-error-fragment\",\n    \"title\": \"Run log general collector failure error fragment rendering lacks regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": true,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:46.221Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: server.go:121 (handleLogs), templates/log.html:18 (error state card), route GET /logs. Behaviors: when GET /logs?instance=\\u003cid\\u003e\\u0026run=\\u003cid\\u003e is requested and Collector.Logs returns a non-exit-4 failure (e.g. process exit 1, I/O error, or timeout), Canopy must return HTTP 200 with the log drawer fragment rendering State = \\\"error\\\", badge \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003eerror\\u003c/span\\u003e, headline \\u003cp\\u003eCanopy could not read this Run log.\\u003c/p\\u003e, and the error message in \\u003cp class=\\\"muted\\\"\\u003e, without returning an HTTP 500 error or panicking. Failing example: configure collector.logs to return errors.New(\\\"ssh connection reset by peer\\\") or \\u0026CLIError{Command: \\\"run logs\\\", Exit: 1, Message: \\\"database disk image is malformed\\\"} and request GET /logs?instance=one\\u0026run=run-1; today server_test.go:37 (TestHandlerRejectsUnknownAndMalformedRun) covers exit 4 (\\\"unknown\\\") and malformed query params, and TestHandlerMapsEvictedLogToFragmentState covers evicted logs, but the general collector error rendering path is unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds a test in server_test.go verifying that when Collector.Logs returns a non-exit-4 error, GET /logs returns HTTP 200, renders state \\\"error\\\" with \\u003cspan class=\\\"signal error\\\"\\u003eerror\\u003c/span\\u003e, and displays the collector error message. Observed: server.go:121-124 assigns view.State = \\\"error\\\" on general collector failure, but grep shows server_test.go never tests GET /logs with a failing collector other than exit 4. Required: an HTTP regression test in server_test.go verifying that general collector errors during log fetching render the error fragment with HTTP 200. Proposed test-work: add a server test in server_test.go verifying that GET /logs returns HTTP 200 and renders the error state fragment when Collector.Logs encounters a non-exit-4 failure.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:50:11.121Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Merged into active canopy-log-drawer-experience. Pinning current inline markup and headline would be obsolete during drawer redesign