{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_621579","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder show canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering\",\n  \"title\": \"Zero-instance empty inventory page and fragment rendering lack regression cover\",\n  \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\",\n  \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"lease\": {\n    \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n    \"principal\": \"none\",\n    \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:19:02.012Z\"\n  },\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:37.391Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:49 (handlePage), server.go:82 (handleInstance), templates/fleet.html:36, templates/instance.html:145. Behaviors: when Canopy runs with zero configured or discovered instances, GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance must return HTTP 200 and gracefully render the empty-state templates (\\\"No instances configured.\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\", \\\"Add an instance to the inventory to begin observing it.\\\") without panic, nil pointer dereference, or HTTP 500. Failing example: initialize NewApp with Inventory{Instances: []} and issue GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance; today all tests in server_test.go initialize testInventory() with one pre-configured instance, leaving the zero-instance empty template rendering path unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in server_test.go with an empty inventory asserting that GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance return HTTP 200, contain the expected empty-state text (\\\"No instances configured\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\"), and do not produce template execution errors. Observed: templates have explicit branches for empty instances (fleet.html:36, instance.html:145), but grep shows no test in server_test.go exercises an empty App inventory. Required: HTTP handler regression tests for empty-inventory page and fragment rendering. Proposed test-work: add server tests verifying that GET /, /fragments/fleet, and /fragments/instance return 200 with empty-state messages when no instances are configured.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"text\": \"took\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\n  \"promotions\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:32.84Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": false,\n    \"takeable\": true\n  }\n}\n"}],"details":{}}}
