{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_621587","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder show canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure\",\n  \"title\": \"Initial instance collection failure unknown freshness and attempted state lack regression cover\",\n  \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\",\n  \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"lease\": {\n    \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n    \"principal\": \"none\",\n    \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:33:53.108Z\"\n  },\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:59:00.096Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: view.go:208-213 (instanceView), view.go:160 (classifyFreshness), templates/instance.html:18 (\\\"Waiting for first observation\\\"). Behaviors: when an instance has never completed a successful collection (e.g. host unreachable or binary failure on first launch), Canopy must maintain its freshness as \\\"unknown\\\" (never \\\"stale\\\" or \\\"fresh\\\"), set Reachable: false, record LastObserved with prefix \\\"attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e\\\", surface the failure in Errors, and render the \\\"Waiting for first observation\\\" card. Failing example: configure an instance whose collector fails immediately on the first attempt without any prior successful snapshot; today TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure in app_test.go only tests failure after an initial success (transitioning to \\\"stale\\\"), leaving the initial-failure path (view.go:210) untested. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test in app_test.go asserting that after an initial refresh failure, app.state(id) has Snapshot == nil, instanceView has Freshness: \\\"unknown\\\", Reachable: false, LastObserved prefixed with \\\"attempted \\\", Errors containing the collector error, and instance.html rendering the waiting-title card. Observed: view.go:210 sets \\\"attempted \\\" when Snapshot is nil and LastAttempt is non-zero, but grep shows \\\"attempted\\\" is never asserted in any test file. Required: a regression test in app_test.go for initial instance collection failure. Proposed test-work: add an app/view regression test proving an instance failing its initial collection reports unknown freshness, attempted timestamp, and the waiting card.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:26:41.534Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"took\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:29:23.983Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"ask: Implementation and checks are complete at f93e178 on forest/canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure/first-failure-proof; PR https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/pull/11. Focused regression, all Go tests, and go vet pass. This executive session has no Runner FOREST_RUN_ID, so it cannot publish authorized Builder review-request evidence. An authorized Builder Run must adopt this exact branch, validate/rebase if needed, and publish forest.review-request.v2 for tracker powder. Do not treat the PR or raw branch push as Gate approval or job completion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:31:26.472Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"text\": \"answer: Executive recovery complete: PR #11 closed and remote forest branch deleted. No review-request evidence was created. Implementation is preserved in the local ref executive/initial-collection-failure-preserved at f93e178. A normal Builder may select this job, inspect/cherry-pick that commit into its own fresh forest branch if useful, rerun checks, and publish through the authorized Runner Gate. Do not treat prior PR or checks as approval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:33:53.108Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"text\": \"took\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\n  \"promotions\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.282Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTests cover a collection failure only after a successful snapshot. They do not defend the stronger first-observation invariant: an instance that has never succeeded is unknown, never fresh or stale, while still showing the failed attempt.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nAfter the first collection attempt fails for an instance with no prior snapshot:\\n\\n- Preserve no successful snapshot and zero `LastSuccess`.\\n- Record `LastAttempt` and the collector error.\\n- Render freshness as `unknown` and reachability as false.\\n- Render `LastObserved` as `attempted \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e`, surface the error, and keep the `Waiting for first observation` state.\\n- Do not start background discovery or depend on host state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nUse a deterministic failing collector for one `refreshOnce`, then exercise the real instance fragment/template. Assert HTTP 200, unknown/first-observation output, attempted timestamp, and visible failure; assert no fresh/stale classification. Existing success-then-failure retention coverage remains unchanged.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:54.638Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:33:53.108Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": false,\n    \"takeable\": true\n  }\n}\n"}],"details":{}}}
