{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"command\":\"powder note canopy-tester-selection-idempotent-trigger --text 'filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788636942913138403-tester (git a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a), running PID 1447309 (build 73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6)\\nSurface: server.go:82-99 (handleInstance), app.go:336-353 (selectInstance), app.go:140 (refreshLoop), route GET /fragments/instance. Behaviors: instance selection state transitions and polling idempotency: (1) when an instance becomes selected (selectInstance switches selection from one instance to another), Canopy must update selectedID(), enqueue a wake signal to the newly selected instance worker to trigger an immediate collection attempt without waiting for the next periodic cycle, and return response header HX-Trigger-After-Swap: canopy-selection on GET /fragments/instance; (2) when the same selected instance is polled again (GET /fragments/instance?instance=<id> or GET /fragments/instance), selectInstance must return false, must not enqueue an unneeded worker wake signal, and must omit HX-Trigger-After-Swap to prevent an infinite HTMX fleet re-query loop; (3) when an unknown instance ID is requested, selectInstance must return false and leave the active selection unchanged. Failing example: issue two consecutive GET /fragments/instance?instance=two requests against app.Handler(); today server_test.go:96 (TestInstanceSelectionTriggersFleetRefresh) only issues a single request and checks that HX-Trigger-After-Swap is present on initial selection change, leaving the idempotent subsequent poll (which must omit the trigger header) unexercised; furthermore app_test.go contains zero tests verifying that selection change wakes the target worker. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in server_test.go and app_test.go verifying that: initial selection change returns HX-Trigger-After-Swap: canopy-selection, repeated polling of the selected instance returns HTTP 200 without HX-Trigger-After-Swap, selectInstance wakes the target worker on change, and selecting an unknown instance returns false without mutating selection. Observed: server.go:91-94 sets the header only when selectionChanged is true and app.go:346-350 gates worker wake on changed, but tests only assert the positive transition once. Required: regression tests in server_test.go and app_test.go covering selection idempotency and worker wake dispatch. Proposed test-work: add server and app tests proving that instance selection change wakes the worker and sets the HTMX trigger while repeat polling omits the trigger and avoids redundant wakeups.' --agent \\\"${POWDER_AGENT:-tester}\\\"\"}"}}
