ng the specific surfaces examined, from `inventory.go`'s parsing logic to `server.go`'s HTTP routing, and I've identified five spec-less draft findings, including one related to declaration collection boundaries.\\n\\n**Documenting Sweep Details**\\n\\nI'm now documenting specific sweep findings and exclusions. I've listed identified issues, like `canopy-tester-selection-idempotent-trigger`, and noted several findings skipped due to duplication or active workstreams, such as envelope schema validation.\\n\\n\",\"format\":\"google-gemini-v1\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Tester Sweep Report\n\n**Worktree:** `1788636942913138403-tester` (Git revision `a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a`)  \n**Deployment:** PID `1447309` (running binary build `73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6`)  \n**Target Repository:** `misty-step/canopy`\n\n---\n\n### 1. Surfaces Checked\n\n- **Collector Protocol & Runner Boundaries (`collector.go`, `collector_test.go`):**  \n  Examined `cliCollector.Collect`, `cliCollector.runJSON`, `decodeCLIEnvelope`, and `decodeCommandData`. Verified coverage of top-level envelope framing (recently landed in `a1673eb`), command mismatches, and exit code handling. Identified gaps in declaration collection boundary validation, subprocess exit/stderr attribution, and context deadline handling.\n- **Application State Transitions & Polling Cadence (`app.go`, `app_test.go`, `freshness_test.go`):**  \n  Examined `selectInstance`, `refreshLoop`, `refreshInterval`, `freshnessWindow`, and `syncDiscoveredInstances`. Checked worker non-overlapping tests, startup discovery worker lifecycles, and freshness cycle budget tests (landed in `73d1489`). Identified gaps in worker wake dispatch on selection transitions and idempotent repeat polling.\n- **HTTP Routing, Fragment Serving & Headers (`server.go`, `server_test.go`):**  \n  Examined route instance/run query parameter validation (landed in `674894f`), method-not-allowed guards, health check endpoint, audit divergence stale overrides (landed in `c203dc9`), and template execution. Identified lack of anti-caching (`Cache-Control: no-store`) regression coverage across HTML pages and HTMX polling fragments.\n- **View Projections & Templates (`view.go`, `templates_test.go`, `templates/*.html`):**  \n  Inspected view model transformations for fleet, instance, triggers, live runs, recent runs, declarations, and ledger agents. Verified document visibility pause triggers for background polling.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Findings Filed (SPEC-LESS Powder Drafts)\n\nFive draft jobs were filed without specs (`takeable: false`), each carrying deployment provenance, concrete surface references, observable behaviors, failing examples, and acceptance criteria:\n\n1. **`canopy-tester-declaration-collection-boundary`**\n   - **Title:** CLI collector declaration list validation, duplicate rejection, and show mismatch lack regression cover\n   - **Surface:** `collector.go:174-207` (`cliCollector.Collect`), methods `declaration list` and `declaration show`\n   - **Observable Behaviors:** Rejection of null/missing `data.declarations`, route identifier traversal validation before dispatching `declaration show`, duplicate declaration name rejection, declaration name mismatch rejection (`declaration.Name != listed.Name`), and fallback to `listed.Name` for legacy Forest CLI builds that omit the repeated name.\n\n2. **`canopy-tester-selection-idempotent-trigger`**\n   - **Title:** Instance selection state transition worker wake and idempotent polling HX-Trigger lack regression cover\n   - **Surface:** `server.go:82-99` (`handleInstance`), `app.go:336-353` (`selectInstance`), `app.go:140` (`refreshLoop`), route `GET /fragments/instance`\n   - **Observable Behaviors:** Waking the target worker and returning header `HX-Trigger-After-Swap: canopy-selection` on an active instance selection switch; omitting the trigger header and avoiding redundant wakeups on repeated polls of the already-selected instance (preventing HTMX fleet re-query loops); returning `false` and preserving selection on unknown IDs.\n\n3. **`canopy-tester-subprocess-error-attribution`**\n   - **Title:** CLI collector empty stdout, stderr error capture, process exit mismatch, and envelope contradiction lack regression cover\n   - **Surface:** `collector.go:283-342` (`cliCollector.runJSON`), `collector.go:394-406` (`commandFailureMessage`)\n   - **Observable Behaviors:** Returning `\"command emitted no JSON envelope\"` on empty stdout with exit 0; capturing subprocess stderr text in the `*CLIError` message on non-zero exit with empty stdout; detecting process exit code vs envelope exit code discrepancies (`\"process exit X does not match envelope exit Y\"`); rejecting exit-0 envelopes with non-null `\"error\"` or null `\"data\"`.\n\n4. **`canopy-tester-collector-timeout-deadline`**\n   - **Title:** CLI collector execution timeout and context cancellation attribution lack regression cover\n   - **Surface:** `collector.go:49-66` (`NewCLICollector`, `NewCLICollectorWithRunner`), `collector.go:289-295` (`runJSON`), `collector.go:138` (`Collect`)\n   - **Observable Behaviors:** Enforcing execution timeout bounds so slow subprocesses time out with a command-attributed `*CLIError` containing `\"context deadline exceeded\"` and exit -1; halting collection promptly upon parent context cancellation; failing closed on nil contexts.\n\n5. **`canopy-tester-cache-control-headers`**\n   - **Title:** HTTP Cache-Control no-store and Content-Type headers across page and fragment routes lack regression cover\n   - **Surface:** `server.go:230-234` (`render`), `server.go:137` (`handleLogs`), routes `GET /`, `GET /fragments/fleet`, `GET /fragments/instance`, and `GET /logs`\n   - **Observable Behaviors:** Ensuring live operator HTML pages and HTMX polling fragments emit `Cache-Control: no-store` and `Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8` to prevent browser history or intermediary proxies from caching live incident data; ensuring `GET /healthz` emits `Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Findings Skipped as Duplicates or Active Workstreams\n\n- **Top-level CLI envelope JSON structure & schema validation:** Skipped; already implemented and proven in `canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation` (commit `a1673eb`).\n- **Inventory listen bounds and negative intervals:** Skipped; previously merged into `if-critic-silent-canopy-config`.\n- **Log text secret redaction:** Skipped; actively tracked in open job `if-critic-log-sanitize-untested`.\n- **Log drawer error fragment markup:** Skipped; actively tracked in open job `canopy-log-drawer-experience`.\n- **Discovery ID collisions & root reconciliation:** Skipped; actively tracked in open job `canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision`.\n- **Discovered instance selection pruning fallback:** Skipped to prevent overlap with active discovery reconciliation revisions under review in `canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision`.\n- **Route instance/run query parameter validation:** Skipped; already implemented and proven in `canopy-tester-route-param-validation` (commit `674894f`).\n- **Audit divergence stale trust override:** Skipped; already implemented and proven in `canopy-tester-audit-divergence-stale` (commit `c203dc9`).\n- **Elapsed freshness decay:** Skipped; already implemented and proven in `canopy-critic-stale-selected-window` (commit `73d1489`).\n- **Zero-instance empty inventory page/fragment rendering:** Skipped; actively tracked in open job `canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering`.\n- **Initial collection failure unknown freshness:** Skipped; actively tracked in open job `canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Findings Discarded for Lack of Concrete Behavioral Evidence\n\n- **Helper duration formatting (`formatDuration` in `view.go`):** Discarded; internal helper unit testing violates the Tester declaration boundary against chasing raw helper unit coverage.\n- **Recent runs and ledger table markup pinning:** Discarded; per established Verifier and Critic feedback on abandoned trigger matrix warnings, standalone suites pinning HTML markup and copied fields add maintenance overhead without demonstrating an independent behavioral defect.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Repository Integrity\n\n- No files modified in the repository.\n- Working tree is clean on commit `a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a`.\n- No branches created, published, committed, or pushed.\n- All five filed Powder jobs remain strictly SPEC-LESS drafts (`takeable: false`)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","usage":{"input":4245,"output":2966,"cacheRead":111282,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":970,"totalTokens":118493,"cost":{"input":0.00403275,"output":0.011864,"cacheRead":0.01780512,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03370187}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788637334449,"responseId":"gen-1788637334-wZUu5zpWNaVL97HeedOB","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
